      "entryType": "HAZARD",
      "name": "Floating Flamethrower",
      "level": 16,
      "rarity": "common",
      "size": "medium",
      "traits": [
        "fire",
        "magical",
        "trap"
      ],
      "description": "A floating skull of fire swoops around the arena, rotating as it weaves through the ring and releasing huge gouts of flame in random directions.",
      "armorClass": 42,
      "hitPoints": 100,
      "hardness": 25,
      "stealth": {
        "modifier": 23,
        "details": "+23 (expert) or check (perception, dc:38, traits:action:seek) (master) to notice the pattern of the orb's trajectory"
      },
      "disable": "three check (thievery, dc:40, name:Disable an Elemental Core, traits:action:disable-a-device,hazard,magical,trap,fire) (legendary) checks or castings of Dispel Magic (7th rank; counteract DC 40), one each to pull out or disable the elemental cores hidden in the floating skull's right eye, left eye, and mouth",
      "isComplex": true,
      "routine": "(3 actions) The trap loses 1 action per turn per successful check to disable. The floating flamethrower uses its first action to release a gout of flame in a 15-foot cone that deals 4d6+4 fire damage (check (reflex, dc:40, basic) save), its second action to fly in a U-shape in a random direction, and its third action to release another gout of flame.",
